{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>For housings for the poles.</b> According to what I explained regarding the rings of the Ark — that one must cast four rings and set them into the Ark, and inside the rings one inserts two rings, and into the rings one places the poles — here it says that one need not do so; rather, the rings themselves that are set in place will serve as housings for the poles. Understand this:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:24.138785203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}